USOS CSMWrap patch 0021 (2026-10-19): USB disk service (UDS) on channel 1 of the helper core

Windows 95/98/98 SE/Me on the X470 have no xHCI driver; SeaBIOS inside
CSMWrap is the only xHCI owner (USB keyboard, mouse and INT 13h). With
csmwrap.ini int13_boot_disk_only = true (patch 0014) a USB stick gets no
BIOS drive number, so the 9x real-mode mapper never touches it. This patch
lets an OS driver (USOSUSB.MPD, a SCSIPORT miniport in the USOS repository)
send SCSI commands to such a stick through SeaBIOS, with no second xHCI
owner (docs/usb9x-hotswap-design-2026-10-19.md, stage 1):

- stacks.c: the "CSMPPrxy" mailbox is 64-byte aligned and gets channel 1
  at +48 (magic "UDS1", req_phys, doorbell, done) in the same cache line,
  so the helper's MONITOR on request_pending also wakes on the doorbell.
  CSMWrap's own copy of the struct (48 bytes) and offsets 0-47 unchanged.
- romlayout.S: the helper loop checks channel 0 first (unchanged), then
  doorbell != done -> usos_uds_service(mailbox + 48).
- hw/usb-uds.c (new): the request block is read once from the OS's
  physical address (refused when 0, unaligned, wrapping or in
  A0000h-FFFFFh), validated (magic, version, size, op, dev, LUN, CDB
  length 6-16, direction, length <= 64 KiB, data range not wrapping and
  not in A0000h-FFFFFh), then ENUM (device table), SCSI (CBW / data / CSW
  with any CDB and direction, automatic REQUEST SENSE on CSW status 1),
  RESET (BOT reset recovery), EJECT (SYNCHRONIZE CACHE, START STOP UNIT
  LoEj; the entry stays ejected until reboot) or STATUS (a copy of the
  record below). Only results are written back, then done = doorbell.
  A device with a BIOS drive number (hard disk or CD-ROM, opt-out of
  0014) is refused (OWNED): never two owners of one file system.
- usb-msc.c: an xHCI BOT device gets a device-table entry at setup
  (up to 8; generation 1, LUNs, root port and slot id; no extra USB
  traffic at POST); its control pipe is kept instead of being put on the
  free list (on xHCI that never released the slot), for the BOT reset
  recovery. VID:PID, INQUIRY vendor/product and READ CAPACITY(10) of LUN 0
  are read on the helper core at the first request for a device without
  a BIOS number. usbdrive_s moves to usb-msc.h with a table index. INT 13h
  use of USB disks is unchanged.
- usb-xhci.c: own bulk TD to a physical buffer (two chained TRBs with
  ISP when it crosses a 64 KiB boundary), checking on every wait pass
  that the controller still answers (capability dword as at POST, not
  all ones, not halted, no host system error) and that the device's root
  port still has CCS: an unplug ends the request at once (GONE), the slot
  gets Disable Slot and stays gone until reboot; endpoint recovery after
  a stall / error / timeout (Reset Endpoint, Stop Endpoint, Set TR
  Dequeue Pointer); BOT reset recovery = Bulk-Only Mass Storage Reset +
  CLEAR_FEATURE(ENDPOINT_HALT) on both bulk endpoints (missing upstream:
  "XXX - reset connection"). No PCI configuration access from the helper
  core (CF8h/CFCh would race the OS on the other CPU), the MMIO checks
  stand in for the BAR check of patch 0010.
- A diagnostics record in low memory (VARLOW, 16-byte aligned, "USOS"
  "UDSK", version 1, 768 bytes, header written at xHCI setup): per device
  state, BIOS number, LUNs, port, VID:PID, slot, speed, generation,
  capacity, last CDB / CSW / sense / status, counters (requests, CHECK,
  timeouts, BOT resets, GONE, refused, KiB in/out); the BIOS hard disks
  and CD-ROMs as mapped (number, DTYPE, UDS index, sectors); a ring of the
  last 16 events (present, gone, reset, eject, bad request, controller
  failure, timeout, phase error, registration failure, stall). Written
  only, for USOSDBG.EXE / USOSLOG.EXE.

Without an OS client nothing calls channel 1 and every other path behaves
as in 3.1.2-usos15.

Own code. Applies after 0001-0010, 0012, 0014-0020, patch -p1 from the
top of the tree. Part of a MODIFIED CSMWrap made by the USOS project
(SeaBIOS LGPLv3).

